Roles and Responsibilities

-	Developers : Implementing the codes and writing them down.
-	Testers : Tests were created by them that included test cases for valid, invalid, and edge case scenarios.
-	Reviewers: They examined the pull requests, left meaningful comments respectively, and approved when all the standards were satisfied.
-	Repository manager: Merged all the pull requests once the approvals were complete.

Conclusion

This full SQA plan tells us how the project’s phase 1 quality has been maintained throughout with the coding standards, design, Javadoc documentation, systematic testing, and Github peer reviews. It was ensured that deliverables have respectable quality, met project requirements, all by the structures review process and comprehensive test coverages.
